[I] Analog style vocoder for JACK

[T] Zita-avc1 is an 'analog' style vocoder inspired by the EMS vocoders of
[T] the 1970s, a standalone application using JACK for audio and MIDI input
[T] and output. It uses two sets of 24 sixth order bandpass filters.

[U] https://kokkinizita.linuxaudio.org/linuxaudio/

[A] Kokkini Zita
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/multimedia
[F] CROSS

[L] GPL3
[V] 0.1.0

[D] 9efdca81706e814adb89fc3cb7393a0d24cf10d64293c6d4f0f4c8e5 zita-avc1-0.1.0.tar.bz2 https://kokkinizita.linuxaudio.org/linuxaudio/downloads/

srcdir=*/source
var_append GCC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' -c?:-L$root$(pkgprefix libdir libxft)
